// ERD for the Cucumber Studio-like BDD platform.
// Owner: pm proposes, backend-swe keeps the as-built part in sync with the JPA entities.
// Legend: blue headers = as-built (auth-service code), orange headers = proposed (approved design 2026-10-12, not yet implemented).
// View: paste into https://dbdiagram.io or open with a DBML plugin. See docs/erd/README.md.

Project cucumber {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
  **As-built at 2026-10-15** (branch staging, auth-service-persistence review point C: Flyway V1 to V7 on PostgreSQL 17; V1 equals Hibernate's PostgreSQL DDL for the original entities). Type notes give the PostgreSQL DDL of the applied migrations. backend-swe keeps this in sync.

  **Conventions (all services)**
  - Primary keys: `id uuid`. auth-service generates them in the application (`@GeneratedValue(strategy = AUTO)` on a UUID field).
  - Names: snake_case tables and columns. Hibernate default naming turns camelCase fields into snake_case, so `seatLimit` becomes `seat_limit`.
  - Timestamps: `created_at` on every table, and `updated_at` on every mutable table. Immutable rows (history, attachments) have only `created_at`. All services use `Instant` stored as `timestamptz` in UTC; as-built in auth-service since V2.
  - Enums are stored as strings (`@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)`) in `varchar(32)` plus a named `CHECK ck_<table>_<column>_values` (ERD-D12). auth-service has this as-built (V4) and has no DBML Enums; each column's note lists its values. The proposed services keep DBML Enums for readability. Values are UPPER_SNAKE_CASE like the Java constants. An API may present execution statuses in lower case (passed, failed, ...), which is a contract decision, not a storage one.
  - Each service owns its own database. **There are no cross-service foreign keys.** A column that points into another service is a plain uuid with a note "references <service>.<table>.id (by ID, no FK)".
  - Within one service, relations are real foreign keys (Ref).

  **Legend**
  - Table note starts with "as-built": the table exists today exactly as described.
  - Table note starts with "proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented": a domain design by pm, approved by the user on 2026-10-12 (ERD-D1..D11). Nothing is built yet.
  - "proposed (auth-service phase 1)" would mark an entity change planned by docs/specs/auth-service.md but not yet in code. **Phase 1 plans none**: its "Will not be touched" list includes every entity in model/. Phase 1 only changes the values written (lower-cased emails, plan FREE, seat_limit 5), and those are noted on the columns.
  - "proposed (auth-service-projects)" marked the entity changes of docs/specs/auth-service-projects.md (E31, E36, E37) and its project rules. All of them are implemented (Batches A2, B and C, 2026-10-13), so no auth_service line carries the marker any more.
  - "proposed (auth-service-persistence)" marks a change of the auth_service group planned by docs/specs/auth-service-persistence.md (Ready, approved by the user 2026-10-14). **All of it is as-built since review point C (2026-10-15), V1 to V7:** PostgreSQL 17 with Flyway; timestamptz/Instant (V2); NOT NULL and lengths (V3); enums as varchar(32) plus named CHECKs, with no auth-service DBML Enums (V4); lower-case email checks and the unique (org_id, lower(name COLLATE "und-x-icu")) index on projects (V5); foreign-key indexes and ON DELETE RESTRICT (V6); audit_log dropped (V7). Any marker still left on an auth_service line is stale.
  - "proposed (report-service)" marks a refinement of the report_service design by docs/specs/report-service.md (Ready, approved by the user on 2026-10-26). It applies on top of the 2026-10-12 design: a new upload_tokens table and test_runs.upload_token_id; feature_version (a number) instead of feature_version_id; snapshot columns as text/jsonb; step arguments on step_results; no database defaults; enums as varchar(32) plus CHECK (ERD-D12); named constraints and ON DELETE RESTRICT (no deletes in phase 1). attachments stays as designed and is not created in phase 1.
  - "proposed (scenario-service)" marks a refinement of the scenario_service design by docs/specs/scenario-service.md (Ready, approved by the user on 2026-10-14). It applies on top of the 2026-10-12 design: jsonb instead of json, names as text, path uniqueness among active features only, tag_assignments.feature_id, enums stored as varchar(32) plus CHECK (ERD-D12), named constraints and delete rules per the database pattern (spec D14), and the id-stability and content rules (spec D8 to D12). The DBML Enums of scenario_service stay for readability; the real columns are varchar(32) with a CHECK, as noted on each column. backend-swe turns the scenario_service tables into as-built when its Flyway V1 migration and entities land (spec T2, T7).

  **Runtime database today (as-built 2026-10-15):** PostgreSQL 17, database auth_service (UTF-8, locale provider builtin, C.UTF-8), schema from Flyway migrations V1 to V7, ddl-auto validate. Tests use a postgres:17 Testcontainers container. H2 is removed. flyway_schema_history is managed by Flyway and not modelled here. Shared conventions for all services: spec section "Database pattern for every service".
  scenario-service starts directly on PostgreSQL 17 (database scenario_service, builtin C.UTF-8) with Flyway migrations and `ddl-auto: validate`, following the same "Database pattern for every service" (docs/specs/scenario-service.md D14); it never uses H2.
  '''
}

// =====================================================================
// AS-BUILT: auth-service (com.example.authservice.model, enums)
// =====================================================================

Table users [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  email varchar(254) [unique, not null, note: 'unique uk_users_email (V1); varchar(254) since V3 (E70), the API limit (E17). The application trims and lower-cases emails before storing and comparing them (D12). CHECK ck_users_email_lower_case (email = lower(email)) since V5 (E72), so the unique constraint is case-insensitive uniqueness.']
  password_hash varchar(255) [null, note: 'explicitly nullable (@Column(nullable = true)); BCrypt hash. Deliberately nullable, for future accounts without a password (auth-service-persistence D8).']
  full_name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'varchar(100) not null since V3 (E70), mirrored by @Column(nullable = false, length = 100); the API limit (E17). The API rejects control characters and lone surrogates (D11 rule T1).']
  status varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum UserStatus, EnumType.STRING; varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_users_status_values (V1): ACTIVE, SUSPENDED, PENDING_VERIFICATION. PENDING_VERIFICATION is set by register and by anonymous invitation acceptance; phase 1 (D4): it may log in, only SUSPENDED is blocked.']
  mfa_enabled boolean [not null, note: 'primitive boolean, so Hibernate adds NOT NULL; no DB default']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set by application code from the service clock (Instant, UTC; V2, E69), no @CreationTimestamp; not null since V3 (E70).']
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set once at register from the service clock (V2, E69); nothing updates it later; not null since V3 (E70).']

  Note: 'as-built (entity User, @Table users)'
}

Table organizations [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'varchar(100) not null since V3 (E70), mirrored by @Column(nullable = false, length = 100). The API limits it to 1-100 non-blank characters (E17); stored as sent; duplicates are allowed.']
  plan varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum Plan, EnumType.STRING; varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_organizations_plan_values (V1): FREE, TEAM, ENTERPRISE. createOrganization sets FREE, the only plan written so far.']
  seat_limit int [null, note: 'Integer; null means unlimited (spec glossary). createOrganization sets app.orgs.free-seat-limit (default 5). Seats used = members + PENDING invitations not yet expired (D11). CHECK ck_organizations_seat_limit_positive (seat_limit IS NULL OR seat_limit > 0) since V3 (E70).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set from the service clock (timestamptz since V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']

  Note: 'as-built (entity Organization, @Table organizations). No updated_at column. Invitations, acceptances, role changes and removals lock this row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) so the seat limit and the last-owner rule hold under concurrent requests.'
}

Table org_memberships [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  org_id uuid [not null]
  role varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum OrganizationRole, EnumType.STRING; varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_org_memberships_role_values (V1): OWNER, ADMIN, MEMBER, READER (ranks 4 to 1, Java-only via isAtLeast, not stored).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set from the service clock (timestamptz since V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']

  indexes {
    (user_id, org_id) [unique, name: 'uk_org_memberships_user_id_org_id', note: 'as-built (V1): unique constraint']
    org_id [name: 'ix_org_memberships_org_id', note: 'as-built (V6, E73): foreign-key index']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (entity OrgMembership). Exactly one role per user and organization. created_at is joinedAt in the member list. Rows are deleted when a member is removed or leaves.'
}

Table projects [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  org_id uuid [not null]
  name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'unique per organization ignoring case, archived projects included: index uk_projects_org_id_name_lower (V5, E72). The API (T11) limits it to 1-100 non-blank characters as sent (counted before trimming), stores it trimmed, and keeps it unique per organization (trimmed, lower-cased with Locale.ROOT, archived projects included) in the application, under the organization row lock. varchar(100) not null since V3 (E70), mirrored by @Column(nullable = false, length = 100).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set from the service clock (timestamptz since V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']
  archived_at timestamptz [null, note: 'set from the service clock when the project is archived, null when active (E31, D5; timestamptz since V2, E69). Archived projects stay readable but are read-only; there is no hard delete.']

  indexes {
    (org_id, `lower(name COLLATE "und-x-icu")`) [unique, name: 'uk_projects_org_id_name_lower', note: 'as-built (V5, E72): archived projects included. ICU lower() matches Java toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT); the builtin C.UTF-8 lower() does not for U+0130 (decided 2026-10-15). The application check under the organization lock stays the primary rule (PROJECT_NAME_TAKEN). Also serves as the index for the org_id foreign key.']
  }

  Note: '''
  as-built (entity Project, Lombok accessors and builder, E31). secret_token was removed (E31, D8): the CI upload token for automated result ingestion (ERD-D2) comes with the result-ingestion spec, hashed with SHA-256, shown once, several per project, revocable, likely as its own table.
  Other services reference projects.id by ID and check access through GET /internal/projects/{projectId}/access (contract C5, ERD-D1; built in auth-service-projects T7).
  Project API under /api/orgs/{orgId}/projects (T11, T12): create, list, view, rename, archive and restore. No hard delete. Every write takes the organization row lock (P13).
  '''
}

Table project_memberships [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  project_id uuid [not null]
  role varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum ProjectRole, EnumType.STRING; varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_project_memberships_role_values (V1): ADMIN, MEMBER, TESTER, READER (ranks 4 to 1, Java-only via isAtLeast, not stored).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set from the service clock (timestamptz since V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']

  indexes {
    (user_id, project_id) [unique, name: 'uk_project_memberships_user_id_project_id', note: 'as-built (V1): unique constraint']
    project_id [name: 'ix_project_memberships_project_id', note: 'as-built (V6, E73): foreign-key index']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (entity ProjectMembership). Read by the effective-role resolver (ProjectRoleService, D3): organization OWNER and ADMIN are implicit project ADMIN without a row, and an organization READER row counts as at most READER.
  Written by the project member API (T13, T14) and by organization changes (T15). Rules, enforced in the application: a row exists only for a current member of the project organization; an organization READER row holds at most READER. Leaving or being removed from the organization deletes the user rows in that organization projects (E38), and a demotion to organization READER lowers higher roles to READER (E39), in the same transaction. Writes take the organization row lock.
  '''
}

Table invitations [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  email varchar(254) [not null, note: 'varchar(254) not null since V3 (E70); lower case guaranteed by CHECK ck_invitations_email_lower_case (email = lower(email)) since V5 (E72). The application trims and lower-cases it (D12).']
  org_id uuid [not null, note: 'required (join column nullable = false, E36): invitations are for organizations only (D7).']
  role varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum OrganizationRole, EnumType.STRING (E37, D7): an organization role only. varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_invitations_role_values (V1): OWNER, ADMIN, MEMBER, READER.']
  invited_by uuid [not null]
  token varchar(255) [unique, not null, note: 'unique uk_invitations_token (V1), not null since V3 (E70); acceptance token (24 random bytes, 32 URL-safe characters), stored in plain text. Returned once, in the create-invitation response.']
  status varchar(32) [not null, note: 'enum InvitationStatus, EnumType.STRING; varchar(32) since V4 (E71), not null since V3 (E70). CHECK ck_invitations_status_values (V1): PENDING, ACCEPTED, REVOKED, EXPIRED. Written: PENDING on create, ACCEPTED on accept, REVOKED on revoke. EXPIRED is never written; expiry is computed from expires_at, so a stored PENDING may already be expired (spec glossary).']
  expires_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'created_at + 7 days, set by the application from the service clock (V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'set from the service clock (timestamptz since V2, E69); not null since V3 (E70).']

  indexes {
    (org_id, email) [name: 'ix_invitations_org_id_email', note: 'as-built (V6, E73): foreign-key index for org_id, also used by the pending-invitation lookups']
    invited_by [name: 'ix_invitations_invited_by', note: 'as-built (V6, E73): foreign-key index']
  }

  Note: '''
  as-built (entity Invitation). Organization-only since E36 (D7): the project_id column, its foreign key and the project branch of the accept flow were removed. There are no project invitations; project members are added directly from the organization (D6).
  "One pending, unexpired invitation per organization and email" (D11) is enforced only in the application, not by a DB constraint. It stays application-only (auth-service-persistence D8 item 7), because "pending" depends on expires_at > now(), which a partial index can't express (spec D8 item 7).
  Accepting locks the row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) before any user or membership is written, so a token is single use (Q5).
  '''
}

// As-built: every auth_service foreign key is named fk_<table>_<column> (V1) and restricts deletes (ON DELETE RESTRICT since V6, E73, spec D8 item 9).
// audit_log and its four foreign keys were dropped by V7 (E74, option B); auth-service-audit creates audit_logs later.
Ref: org_memberships.user_id > users.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: org_memberships.org_id > organizations.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: projects.org_id > organizations.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: project_memberships.user_id > users.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: project_memberships.project_id > projects.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: invitations.org_id > organizations.id [delete: restrict]
Ref: invitations.invited_by > users.id [delete: restrict]

TableGroup auth_service {
  users
  organizations
  org_memberships
  projects
  project_memberships
  invitations
}

// =====================================================================
// AS-BUILT (schema): scenario-service (Gherkin content), Flyway V1__create_scenario_service_schema.sql (spec T2, 2026-10-18)
// The tables below are exactly V1 on PostgreSQL 17 (database scenario_service, builtin C.UTF-8). Design: docs/specs/scenario-service.md
// (D8 to D14, D19, D20). The JPA entities exist since spec T7 and mirror V1 (review point B passed 2026-10-18). Notes marked "as-built (V1)" describe V1 and the rules it serves.
// Storage per ERD-D12: every enum column below is varchar(32) + CHECK ck_<table>_<column>_values, not a PostgreSQL ENUM type;
// the DBML Enums stay for readability. No column has a database default: the application sets every value (pattern item 11).
// =====================================================================

Enum scenario_kind {
  BACKGROUND [note: 'as-built (V1): CHECK ck_scenarios_kind_values. Background steps are not a test case on their own.']
  SCENARIO [note: 'Scenario or Example keyword']
  SCENARIO_OUTLINE [note: 'Scenario Outline or Scenario Template keyword; has examples']
}

Enum step_keyword {
  GIVEN [note: 'as-built (V1): CHECK ck_steps_keyword_values']
  WHEN
  THEN
  AND
  BUT
  ASTERISK [note: 'the * bullet keyword']
}

Enum step_argument_type {
  NONE [note: 'as-built (V1): CHECK ck_steps_argument_type_values']
  DATA_TABLE
  DOC_STRING
}

Enum tag_target_type {
  FEATURE [note: 'as-built (V1): CHECK ck_tag_assignments_target_type_values']
  RULE
  SCENARIO [note: 'also used for Scenario Outline']
  EXAMPLES
}

Table features [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  path varchar(1024) [not null, note: 'path of the .feature file in the project, e.g. features/checkout/payment.feature. Replaces a folder table in the MVP. as-built (V1): stored as sent; relative POSIX path ending in .feature, no leading /, no empty, . or .. segment, no backslash or control character (spec D10). Can change on a save; a path change alone creates no version. as-built (V1): no segment and no file name before .feature made only of Unicode-blank characters, and no leading Unicode-blank character (spec D10, D20 #4). Case-insensitive comparison = PostgreSQL lower(path COLLATE "und-x-icu"), as in the unique index below.']
  name text [not null, note: 'text after Feature: in the current version. as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(500), and may be empty (Cucumber accepts "Feature:" without a name).']
  description text [not null, note: 'as the parser reports it (leading indentation kept). as-built (V1): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7).']
  language varchar(10) [not null, note: 'from the Gherkin # language: header (en when there is none). The longest dialect code must fit (spec A10). as-built (V1): no database default; the application always sets it.']
  current_version int [not null, note: 'feature_versions.version that the parsed tables (rules, scenarios, steps, examples) reflect']
  created_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  updated_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK). as-built (V1): not null, because create sets it to the creator (spec AC-1.1, D19 #3; database pattern item 10).']
  archived_at timestamptz [null, note: 'soft delete: results in report_service keep pointing at this id. as-built (V1): archived features are read-only, hidden from default lists and the tag catalogue, and free their path; restore clears this (spec D11).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, `md5(lower(path COLLATE "und-x-icu"))`) [unique, name: 'uk_features_project_id_path_lower', note: 'as-built (V1): replaces the plain unique (project_id, path); its leading project_id also serves the feature list. In PostgreSQL it is a PARTIAL unique index: UNIQUE (project_id, md5(lower(path COLLATE "und-x-icu"))) WHERE archived_at IS NULL. as-built (V1): md5 because a valid 1,024-character path of 4-byte characters (4,104 bytes) exceeds the 2,704-byte B-tree entry limit; md5 and lower are IMMUTABLE; equal lower-cased paths always have equal hashes (spec D14). DBML cannot express the WHERE clause, so SQL generated from this file is stricter than the real index (it would also block archived paths). as-built (V1): ICU lower(), as auth_service uk_projects_org_id_name_lower, because the builtin C.UTF-8 lower() differs from Java for U+0130. The application path check uses this same expression, so FEATURE_PATH_TAKEN and the index always agree (spec D10, D20 #1).']
    project_id [name: 'ix_features_project_id', note: 'as-built (V1): feature list per project, including archived features (the partial unique index covers only active ones)']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12).
  One Gherkin file. The Gherkin text in feature_versions is the source of truth. The rules, scenarios, steps, examples and example_rows tables are a parse of the current version only, kept for search, tag filtering and linking results (ERD-D3, ERD-D4).
  as-built (V1): path uniqueness is case-insensitive and only among active features (partial unique index above). Concurrent writes in one project are serialised with a transaction-scoped PostgreSQL advisory lock keyed by project_id (there is no project row in this database).
  Living documentation = the current version of each non-archived feature plus the latest result per scenario. It is computed and needs no table in the MVP. Later: a doc_releases table (a named map of feature_id to version) for published snapshots.
  '''
}

Table feature_versions [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  version int [not null, note: 'starts at 1, +1 on every saved change']
  source text [not null, note: 'full Gherkin text of the file at this version. as-built (V1): stored exactly as sent (line endings and trailing spaces kept), at most 1,000,000 code points, never containing U+0000 or a lone surrogate (spec D8).']
  content_hash varchar(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 hex of source; saving identical content creates no new version. as-built (V1): hash of the UTF-8 bytes of source.']
  message varchar(500) [null, note: 'optional change message; blank is stored as null. as-built (V1): trimmed of Unicode-blank characters before storing, null when nothing is left; no control character or lone surrogate (spec D19 #9).']
  created_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (feature_id, version) [unique, name: 'uk_feature_versions_feature_id_version', note: 'as-built (V1): unique constraint; also indexes the feature_id foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). Immutable history of a feature. A diff between versions is computed from source, not stored. Later: import from Git (commit SHA per version) as a column. as-built (V1): rows are never updated or deleted; a save is refused with VERSION_CONFLICT unless its base version equals features.current_version (spec D9).'
}

Table rules [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  keyword_text text [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Rule (localised languages differ). as-built (V1, widened in place 2026-10-18 by user decision): text, because Gherkin dialect keywords exceed 50 code points (en-tx Examples has 53; spec A10).']
  name text [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(500); may be empty']
  description text [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null, note: 'order among the children of the feature']
  line int [not null, note: 'line number in the current version source. as-built (V1): not null; the parser reports a line for every element (database pattern item 10, spec D20 #9).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]


  indexes {
    feature_id [name: 'ix_rules_feature_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). A Gherkin Rule (Gherkin 6+) that groups a Background and scenarios. as-built (V1): rule ids are not stable across versions; clients must not keep them (spec D9).'
}

Table scenarios [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null, note: 'stable across versions when the scenario is matched on re-parse (ERD-D3); results reference it. as-built (V1): matched by kind (BACKGROUND, SCENARIO, SCENARIO_OUTLINE), name and container (the feature, or a rule with the same name); with duplicate names the n-th old element matches the n-th new one (spec D9).']
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  rule_id uuid [null, note: 'set when the scenario or background sits inside a Rule']
  kind scenario_kind [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_scenarios_kind_values (ERD-D12)']
  keyword_text text [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Scenario, Example, Scenario Outline, Background. as-built (V1, widened in place 2026-10-18 by user decision): text (spec A10).']
  name text [not null, note: 'a Background may have no name. as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(1000); not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7).']
  description text [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null, note: 'order within the feature or rule']
  line int [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null; the parser reports a line for every element (spec D20 #9)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]


  indexes {
    feature_id [name: 'ix_scenarios_feature_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
    rule_id [name: 'ix_scenarios_rule_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12).
  Holds Backgrounds, Scenarios and Scenario Outlines in one table so that steps have one parent. Rule enforced by the application: at most one BACKGROUND per feature and per rule.
  A **test case** is not stored: it is a SCENARIO, or one example row of a SCENARIO_OUTLINE (ERD-D5).
  '''
}

Table steps [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  scenario_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null]
  keyword step_keyword [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_steps_keyword_values (ERD-D12)']
  keyword_text text [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Given, Soit (localised). as-built (V1): without trailing whitespace; text since the in-place widening of 2026-10-18 (user decision, spec A10).']
  step_text text [not null, note: 'step text without the keyword; may contain <placeholders> in outlines']
  argument_type step_argument_type [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_steps_argument_type_values (ERD-D12); no database default, the application always sets it (NONE when the step has no argument).']
  data_table jsonb [null, note: 'when DATA_TABLE: array of rows, each an array of cell strings. as-built (V1): jsonb instead of json.']
  doc_string text [null, note: 'when DOC_STRING: content between the delimiters']
  doc_string_media_type text [null, note: 'optional media type after the opening delimiter, e.g. json. as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(100); the parser accepts any length, and every text it accepts must be storable (spec D8, D20 #9).']
  line int [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null; the parser reports a line for every element (spec D20 #9)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]


  indexes {
    scenario_id [name: 'ix_steps_scenario_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). A step has at most one argument: a data table or a doc string (ERD-D6). Later: a step definition library for autocomplete, kept in a table note until needed. as-built (V1): step ids are not stable across versions; report_service.step_results relies on its text snapshot (spec D9).'
}

Table examples [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  scenario_id uuid [not null, note: 'must be a SCENARIO_OUTLINE (application rule)']
  keyword_text text [not null, note: 'Examples or Scenarios, as written. as-built (V1, widened in place 2026-10-18 by user decision): text, because the en-tx Examples keyword has 53 code points (spec A10).']
  name text [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(500); not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  description text [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null]
  header jsonb [not null, note: 'array of column names, e.g. ["user","result"]. as-built (V1): jsonb instead of json; [] when the Examples block has no table (spec D19 #7).']
  line int [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null; the parser reports a line for every element (spec D20 #9)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]


  indexes {
    scenario_id [name: 'ix_examples_scenario_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). One Examples block of a Scenario Outline. Can carry its own tags. as-built (V1): examples ids are not stable across versions (spec D9).'
}

Table example_rows [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null, note: 'referenced by results; one row = one test case. as-built (V1): kept across versions when the outline keeps its id, the Examples block has the same header, and an old row has identical cells (each old row matches at most one new row, in order); a changed row gets a new id (spec D9).']
  examples_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null]
  cells jsonb [not null, note: 'array of cell strings, same length as examples.header. as-built (V1): jsonb instead of json.']
  line int [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): not null; the parser reports a line for every element (spec D20 #9)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]


  indexes {
    examples_id [name: 'ix_example_rows_examples_id', note: 'as-built (V1): indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). Kept as rows, not JSON inside examples, because each row is a test case that results point to.'
}

Table tags [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name text [not null, note: 'with the leading @, e.g. @smoke; compared case-sensitively like Cucumber tag expressions. as-built (V1): text instead of varchar(255), so any tag the parser accepts can be stored (spec D8, D19 #5). One assignment per element even when the text repeats a tag (D19 #11).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, `md5(name)`) [unique, name: 'uk_tags_project_id_name', note: 'as-built (V1): md5(name) instead of name, because a valid long tag (for example 1,000 emoji) exceeds the 2,704-byte B-tree entry limit. Exact, case-sensitive uniqueness per project is unchanged (spec D12, D14).']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). Project-wide tag catalogue for filtering and autocomplete. Tags are written in the Gherkin text; this table is derived on parse (ERD-D7).
  as-built (V1): the API lists only tags used in an active feature's current version, with the number of such features (featureCount). Whether a row with no assignment left is deleted or kept is an implementation choice (spec D12). Inserts run under the project advisory lock, so two saves introducing one new tag can't collide.
  '''
}

Table tag_assignments [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  tag_id uuid [not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): the feature whose current version carries the tag, whatever the target_type. Makes featureCount, the tag filter and clean-up on re-parse simple queries, and cascades with the feature.']
  target_type tag_target_type [not null, note: 'as-built (V1): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_tag_assignments_target_type_values (ERD-D12)']
  target_id uuid [not null, note: 'id in features, rules, scenarios or examples depending on target_type. Polymorphic, so no FK; the parser keeps it consistent.']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (tag_id, target_type, target_id) [unique, name: 'uk_tag_assignments_tag_id_target_type_target_id', note: 'as-built (V1): unique constraint; also indexes the tag_id foreign key']
    (target_type, target_id) [name: 'ix_tag_assignments_target_type_target_id']
    (feature_id, tag_id) [name: 'ix_tag_assignments_feature_id_tag_id', note: 'as-built (V1): tag catalogue counts and the feature list tag filter; also indexes the feature_id foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (scenario-service V1, 2026-10-18; designed 2026-10-12). Which element carries which tag. Inherited tags (feature to scenario) are computed, not stored.'
}

Ref: feature_versions.feature_id > features.id [delete: restrict] // as-built (V1): restrict, was cascade; versions are never deleted (spec D9, D14)
Ref: rules.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: scenarios.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: scenarios.rule_id > rules.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: steps.scenario_id > scenarios.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: examples.scenario_id > scenarios.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: example_rows.examples_id > examples.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: tag_assignments.tag_id > tags.id [delete: restrict] // as-built (V1): restrict, was cascade; a catalogue row is only removed once unused (spec D12, D14)
Ref: tag_assignments.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade] // as-built (V1)

TableGroup scenario_service {
  features
  feature_versions
  rules
  scenarios
  steps
  examples
  example_rows
  tags
  tag_assignments
}

// =====================================================================
// AS-BUILT (schema): report-service (test runs and results), Flyway V1__create_report_service_schema.sql (spec T2,
// 2026-10-29) -- owner is decision ERD-D2. The six phase-1 tables below are exactly V1 on PostgreSQL 17 (database
// report_service, builtin C.UTF-8), with JPA entities in org.reportservice.model. attachments stays PROPOSED (not in V1).
// Refined by "proposed (report-service)" = docs/specs/report-service.md phase 1 (Ready, approved by the user on 2026-10-26).
// Phase 1 storage per ERD-D12: every enum column is varchar(32) + CHECK ck_<table>_<column>_values; the DBML Enums stay
// for readability. proposed (report-service): no column has a database default; the application sets every value.
// =====================================================================

Enum execution_status {
  PASSED [note: 'as-built (V1, whole enum): varchar(32) + CHECK, Java enum org.reportservice.enums.ExecutionStatus. Cucumber statuses, stored upper case.']
  FAILED
  SKIPPED
  PENDING
  UNDEFINED
  AMBIGUOUS
  UNKNOWN [note: 'not executed yet, e.g. a planned manual test case. Same name as the Cucumber messages status (ERD-D8). proposed (report-service): also the status of an automated test case with no step or hook (spec D9).']
}

Enum test_run_source {
  MANUAL [note: 'as-built (V1, whole enum): varchar(32) + CHECK, Java enum org.reportservice.enums.TestRunSource. Testers record results by hand.']
  AUTOMATED [note: 'results uploaded from a Cucumber run, e.g. by CI']
}

Enum test_run_status {
  PLANNED [note: 'as-built (V1, whole enum): varchar(32) + CHECK, Java enum org.reportservice.enums.TestRunStatus']
  IN_PROGRESS
  COMPLETED
  CANCELLED
}

Enum step_result_kind {
  STEP [note: 'as-built (V1, whole enum): varchar(32) + CHECK, Java enum org.reportservice.enums.StepResultKind']
  BEFORE_HOOK
  AFTER_HOOK
}

Table environments [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'e.g. staging, production, Chrome 129. proposed (report-service): exact, case-sensitive match; created on first use by a run or an upload (spec D11).']
  description text [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): never set in phase 1 (no environment management API yet)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, name) [unique, name: 'uk_environments_project_id_name', note: 'proposed (report-service): named; also serves project_id lookups']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29). Where a test run executed. Later: key/value attributes (browser, OS) as a json column. proposed (report-service): find-or-create under the project advisory lock (spec D11).'
}

Table builds [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(255) [not null, note: 'build or version label, e.g. 1.4.2+517. proposed (report-service): exact, case-sensitive match (spec D11).']
  branch varchar(255) [null]
  commit_sha varchar(64) [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): 4-64 hexadecimal characters, stored lower case (spec D11)']
  ci_url varchar(2048) [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): absolute http or https URL']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, name) [unique, name: 'uk_builds_project_id_name', note: 'proposed (report-service): named']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29). The software build under test. Several runs (environments) can share one build. proposed (report-service): created on first use; branch, commit_sha and ci_url are taken from the first run that names the build and never changed later (spec D11).'
}

Table upload_tokens [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'label chosen by the project ADMIN, e.g. GitHub Actions main; 1-100 code points, not blank, no control character']
  token_hash char(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 hex (lower case) of the full token text; the token itself is never stored or logged (auth-service-projects D8)']
  token_prefix varchar(16) [not null, note: 'the first 12 characters of the token (rct_ plus 8), shown in lists so people can tell tokens apart']
  created_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  expires_at timestamptz [null, note: 'optional; a token is usable while expires_at is null or in the future']
  last_used_at timestamptz [null, note: 'set by each successful upload, in its transaction']
  revoked_at timestamptz [null, note: 'set once by revoke; a revoked token never works again']
  revoked_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    token_hash [unique, name: 'uk_upload_tokens_token_hash']
    project_id [name: 'ix_upload_tokens_project_id']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29). proposed (report-service): new table (spec D4, D5). A per-project CI upload token: 32 random bytes, shown once, stored only as a hash, several per project (at most 10 active), revocable, optional expiry. No hard delete. Replaces the removed auth_service projects.secret_token.'
}

Table test_runs [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(255) [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): 1-255 code points, not blank, no control character']
  source test_run_source [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_test_runs_source_values']
  status test_run_status [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): no database default (was PLANNED); varchar(32) + CHECK ck_test_runs_status_values. MANUAL runs start PLANNED; AUTOMATED runs are created COMPLETED (spec D8).']
  environment_id uuid [null]
  build_id uuid [null]
  tag_expression varchar(1000) [null, note: 'Cucumber tag expression that selected the scope, e.g. @smoke and not @wip. proposed (report-service): phase 1 stores only a single tag (e.g. @smoke) for MANUAL runs; full expressions come later.']
  upload_token_id uuid [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): the token that uploaded an AUTOMATED run; null for MANUAL runs']
  created_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); null when uploaded with a project token']
  started_at timestamptz [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): MANUAL: the first recorded result; AUTOMATED: null in phase 1']
  finished_at timestamptz [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): MANUAL: complete or cancel; AUTOMATED: the upload time']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_test_runs_project_id_created_at', note: 'proposed (report-service): named; the run list, newest first']
    environment_id [name: 'ix_test_runs_environment_id', note: 'proposed (report-service): foreign-key index']
    build_id [name: 'ix_test_runs_build_id', note: 'proposed (report-service): foreign-key index']
    upload_token_id [name: 'ix_test_runs_upload_token_id', note: 'proposed (report-service): foreign-key index']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29).
  One execution of a set of test cases. MANUAL runs are created with one test_case_results row per selected test case in status UNKNOWN; AUTOMATED runs are created from an uploaded result file.
  Reports (pass rate, trends, per tag) are computed from runs and results; no report table in the MVP. Later: denormalised status counters on this table if queries get slow, and saved report filters.
  '''
}

Table test_case_results [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_run_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null, note: 'order in the run']
  feature_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.features.id (by ID, no FK); null when an uploaded result matches no known feature']
  feature_version int [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): replaces feature_version_id uuid. scenario_service.feature_versions.version of feature_id (by value, no FK), the version planned for a MANUAL run; scenario-service exposes version numbers, not version ids. Null for AUTOMATED results in phase 1 (spec D6).']
  scenario_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.scenarios.id (by ID, no FK). proposed (report-service): set for MANUAL results; null for AUTOMATED results in phase 1 (spec D6).']
  example_row_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.example_rows.id (by ID, no FK); set for Scenario Outline test cases']
  feature_path text [not null, note: 'snapshot at run time, so history survives edits and deletions. proposed (report-service): text; MANUAL = the scenario-service path, AUTOMATED = the Cucumber JSON uri as sent (at most 4,096 code points, spec D9).']
  feature_name text [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): new snapshot column; the Feature name (may be empty); groups the run summary per feature']
  scenario_name text [not null, note: 'snapshot; for outlines, the name with placeholders filled in. proposed (report-service): text, as scenario_service names']
  tags jsonb [not null, note: 'snapshot: array of tag names incl. inherited ones. proposed (report-service): jsonb, not null, [] when none; each tag once, at its first position']
  line int [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): new snapshot column; the scenario or example-row line in the feature file']
  status execution_status [not null, note: 'worst step status using the Cucumber precedence; set by hand for MANUAL runs. proposed (report-service): no database default; varchar(32) + CHECK ck_test_case_results_status_values']
  attempt int [not null, note: 'retry number for automated reruns. proposed (report-service): no database default; always 1 in phase 1 (a rerun in one upload is a separate result); rerun grouping comes later (spec D9)']
  executed_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); the tester for MANUAL runs']
  comment text [null, note: 'tester remark for MANUAL runs. proposed (report-service): at most 2,000 code points']
  started_at timestamptz [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): null in phase 1']
  finished_at timestamptz [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): MANUAL: when the status was last recorded; AUTOMATED: null']
  duration_ms bigint [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (test_run_id, position) [unique, name: 'uk_test_case_results_test_run_id_position', note: 'proposed (report-service): unique and named; also indexes the test_run_id foreign key']
    scenario_id [name: 'ix_test_case_results_scenario_id', note: 'proposed (report-service): named; for the later "latest result per scenario"']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29). The result of one test case (a scenario, or one example row of an outline) in one run. proposed (report-service): AUTOMATED results are unlinked snapshots in phase 1 (feature_id, feature_version, scenario_id, example_row_id null); linking is a later phase (spec D6).'
}

Table step_results [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_case_result_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null, note: 'order of execution, including background steps and hooks']
  kind step_result_kind [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): no database default; varchar(32) + CHECK ck_step_results_kind_values']
  step_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.steps.id (by ID, no FK); null for hooks or unmatched steps. proposed (report-service): never set in phase 1 (step ids are not stable, scenario-service D9)']
  keyword_text text [null, note: 'snapshot. proposed (report-service): text, because dialect keywords exceed 50 code points (scenario-service A10); null for hooks']
  step_text text [null, note: 'snapshot with outline placeholders filled in; null for hooks']
  data_table jsonb [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): new snapshot column; array of rows of cell strings, placeholders filled in; null when the step has none']
  doc_string text [null, note: 'proposed (report-service): new snapshot column; null when the step has none']
  status execution_status [not null, note: 'proposed (report-service): no database default; varchar(32) + CHECK ck_step_results_status_values. MANUAL: UNKNOWN in phase 1 (results are recorded per test case)']
  duration_ms bigint [null]
  error_message text [null, note: 'failure message and stack trace as reported by Cucumber. proposed (report-service): truncated to its first 65,536 code points (spec D9)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (test_case_result_id, position) [unique, name: 'uk_step_results_test_case_result_id_position', note: 'proposed (report-service): unique and named; also indexes the foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (V1, report-service T2, 2026-10-29). Per-step status. Background steps appear here as ordinary steps of each test case, as in Cucumber output. proposed (report-service): written once (manual step snapshots, or uploaded steps and hooks) and not changed in phase 1.'
}

Table attachments [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_case_result_id uuid [not null]
  step_result_id uuid [null, note: 'set when attached to a step (screenshots, logs)']
  media_type varchar(255) [not null, note: 'e.g. image/png; logs use text/x.cucumber.log+plain']
  file_name varchar(255) [null]
  size_bytes bigint [not null]
  content bytea [not null, note: 'MVP: stored in the DB with a size cap (ERD-D9). Later: object storage with a storage_key column instead.']
  created_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); null for automated uploads']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    test_case_result_id
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Screenshots, logs and other files attached to a test case or step result. Immutable. proposed (report-service): NOT created in phase 1; uploaded embeddings are ignored until a later phase (spec D1, D9).'
}

// proposed (report-service): phase 1 deletes nothing, so every report_service foreign key restricts deletes and is named fk_<table>_<column> (database pattern). The attachments Refs stay as designed (not built in phase 1).
Ref: test_runs.environment_id > environments.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (report-service): restrict, was set null
Ref: test_runs.build_id > builds.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (report-service): restrict, was set null
Ref: test_runs.upload_token_id > upload_tokens.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (report-service): new
Ref: test_case_results.test_run_id > test_runs.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (report-service): restrict, was cascade
Ref: step_results.test_case_result_id > test_case_results.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (report-service): restrict, was cascade
Ref: attachments.test_case_result_id > test_case_results.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: attachments.step_result_id > step_results.id [delete: cascade]

TableGroup report_service {
  environments
  builds
  upload_tokens
  test_runs
  test_case_results
  step_results
  attachments
}
